WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.286 --> 00:00:11.899
In India it is the khata.

2
00:00:12.179 --> 00:00:13.809
In Mexico, fiado.

3
00:00:14.089 --> 00:00:15.689
In the Philippines, utang.

4
00:00:15.969 --> 00:00:17.230
In Kenya, deni.

5
00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:22.792
The book gets lost, the sums go wrong, and asking a regular customer for money is awkward.

6
00:00:28.299 --> 00:00:31.143
A shopkeeper picks the language they speak in the shop,

7
00:00:31.143 --> 00:00:32.126
and their currency.

8
00:00:32.406 --> 00:00:35.711
The app is honest about which languages run on the device,

9
00:00:35.711 --> 00:00:37.078
and which need a signal.

10
00:00:38.378 --> 00:00:39.470
Then they just say it.

11
00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:42.795
Maria took two loaves of bread and a carton of milk,

12
00:00:42.795 --> 00:00:44.142
six dollars, on credit.

13
00:00:44.422 --> 00:00:48.633
Gemini Nano, running inside Chrome, turns that into a clean entry.

14
00:00:48.913 --> 00:00:50.523
No server, and no cost.

15
00:00:50.803 --> 00:00:53.214
The card shows exactly where it was understood.

16
00:00:54.514 --> 00:00:55.789
Tab adds it all up.

17
00:00:56.069 --> 00:00:58.560
Who owes you, how much, and what came in this week.

18
00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:01.547
Every entry in this book was read on this device.

19
00:01:02.847 --> 00:01:04.740
Same app, a shop in Mexico.

20
00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:06.864
Spanish is read on the device too.

21
00:01:07.144 --> 00:01:10.629
And an English line underneath means anyone can check the entry.

22
00:01:11.929 --> 00:01:13.900
A shop in Nairobi speaks Swahili.

23
00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:20.581
Chrome's on-device model cannot read Swahili yet, so Firebase AI Logic sends it to Gemini in

24
00:01:20.581 --> 00:01:21.277
the cloud.

25
00:01:21.557 --> 00:01:22.433
Same card.

26
00:01:22.713 --> 00:01:23.938
In under three seconds.

27
00:01:25.238 --> 00:01:27.309
Most shops already have years of paper.

28
00:01:27.589 --> 00:01:29.072
Take a photo of a page.

29
00:01:29.352 --> 00:01:33.004
Tab reads it on the device, line by line, free and private.

30
00:01:33.284 --> 00:01:35.777
A crossed-out line is one tap to leave out.

31
00:01:36.057 --> 00:01:39.044
Or read the page in the cloud, in about three seconds.

32
00:01:40.344 --> 00:01:44.931
When it is time to collect, Tab drafts a polite reminder in the shop's own language.

33
00:01:45.211 --> 00:01:46.658
Tab never sends anything.

34
00:01:46.938 --> 00:01:48.379
The shopkeeper decides.

35
00:01:49.679 --> 00:01:51.059
And no signal is fine.

36
00:01:51.339 --> 00:01:55.173
Entries save straight to the device with Firestore's offline cache,

37
00:01:55.173 --> 00:01:57.291
and sync when the network comes back.

38
00:01:58.591 --> 00:01:59.431
Under the hood.

39
00:01:59.711 --> 00:02:03.879
Firebase AI Logic with hybrid inference: on the device first,

40
00:02:03.879 --> 00:02:05.587
the cloud when it has to.

41
00:02:05.867 --> 00:02:07.603
App Check on every AI call.

42
00:02:07.883 --> 00:02:10.620
Anonymous sign-in, so there is no account to make.

43
00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:13.810
And security rules keep every shop's book private.

44
00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:17.585
Tab is live today as a real product.

45
00:02:17.865 --> 00:02:21.620
A site that explains it, a one-click demo book anyone can try,

46
00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:22.771
and the app itself.

47
00:02:23.051 --> 00:02:24.436
Free, with no sign-up.

